% The lab bibliography. This file is the source of truth for the publications
% on the site: edit it, then run
%
%     python3 scripts/build_publications.py
%
% which regenerates _data/publications.yml, the file Jekyll renders from.
% (GitHub Pages cannot parse BibTeX itself - jekyll-scholar is not on its
% allowed-plugin list - so the YAML is a build artifact that gets committed.)
%
% Newest first. Beyond the usual BibTeX fields, these are read by the site:
%
%   venue      short name shown on the page, e.g. CHI, ACL, ACM TOCHI
%   month      jan..dec - sorts papers within a year. Use the month the venue
%              met, not the day the publisher posted it, so a conference's
%              papers stay together. Preprints are dated from the arXiv id.
%   keywords   peer-review | non-peer-review  (non-peer-review gets the pill
%              and files the paper under the Preprints tab)
%   badge      overrides the "Preprint" pill, e.g. Workshop
%   award      adds an award pill, e.g. Best Paper Honorable Mention
%   authorline overrides the printed author line, for 30-author papers
%   selected   true = pin to the homepage list
%
% Link fields - each becomes a button, in this order:
%
%   pdf   a bare filename means resources/paper/pdf/<name>, or a full URL
%   arxiv a bare 2602.04047 means arxiv.org/abs/<id>, or a full URL. Hidden
%         once the paper is published and has a pdf or doi to link instead -
%         the id stays here for citations either way.
%   code  video  demo  data  slides  poster  talk  blog  website  doi
%
% Lab members are bolded automatically from _data/people.yml - never write
% markup into the author field.

